\documentclass{article}
\title{Streaming Speech Recognition on Edge Devices}
\author{L. Marchetti}
\date{March 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Compression}
Quantising the encoder to eight bit precision halves the memory footprint.
Across our test suite we observe \textbf{a 30% reduction} in real time factor
with no statistically significant change in word error rate.
Latency improves most on long utterances,
which makes the quantised model attractive for meeting transcription.
\end{document}

